      "content": "Apologies for the goblin misstep! Let's dive into the nitty-gritty of your trip, sans the mythical creatures.\n\nTraveling from Tokyo to Osaka via Shinkansen is a breeze. The journey takes about 2 hours and 20 minutes, and the cost for a one-way ticket is around ¥3,000. For a round trip, you're looking at about ¥6,000. The Shinkansen is punctual, reliable, and offers a comfortable ride with plenty of amenities.\n\nNow, if you opt for domestic flights, the travel time is significantly shorter. A flight from Tokyo to Osaka takes about 45 minutes, but don't forget the airport security, boarding, and potential delays. The cost of a round-trip flight can vary widely depending on the time of booking and airline, but you might expect to spend around ¥10,000 to ¥20,000 for a round trip.\n\nFrom Osaka to Fukuoka, the Shinkansen takes about 3 hours and 30 minutes, costing around ¥3,000 for a one-way ticket. For a round trip, that's about ¥6,000. If you choose to fly, the journey is even shorter, taking about 1 hour and 30 minutes. However,",
